=== PE 907: Stacking Cups Analysis ===

Tower model: rooted tree. Each cup (except root)
is stacked on exactly one parent below it.

Stacking rules (below → above):
  1. Nesting:     C_k(up) → C_{k+1}(up)     [diff=+1]
  2. Base-to-base: C_k(down) → C_{k±2}(up)   [|diff|=2]
  3. Rim-to-rim:   C_k(up) → C_{k±2}(down)   [|diff|=2]
  Restriction: no double rim-to-rim on same cup

=== Brute force for small n ===
S(1) = 2
S(2) = 1
S(3) = 4
S(4) = 9
S(5) = 14

=== Known values from problem ===
S(4)  = 12
S(8)  = 58
S(20) = 5560

=== Structure ===
Cups of same parity (even/odd) interact via diff=2 rules.
Adjacent cups interact via nesting.
The recurrence can be solved via generating functions.
